== is the incumbent flattered? protobuf-java's memoized serialized size ==
java.version=17.0.20  protobuf-java=protobuf-java-3.25.5.jar
pool=24 freshly parsed messages per round, rounds=9  sink=6270184800

`size cold` is getSerializedSize() on a message that has never been
serialised; `size warm` is the same call once it is memoized; `write` is
writeTo into a buffer the caller owns, which is what the bench's `pbj` arm
measures on iteration 2 and after.

A loop over ONE message therefore reports `write` where an application
that serialises each message once pays `size cold` + `write`. The last
column is the correction the bench's pbj column needs.

